1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,693
Characters, actions, places, occupations, and events in this series are fictional and created for entertainment purposes only.

2
00:00:06,693 --> 00:00:10,920
They are not intended to urge or promote any behavior in the series.

3
00:00:10,920 --> 00:00:13,114
Viewer discretion is advised.

4
00:00:13,114 --> 00:00:14,568
You just got in trouble for fighting.

5
00:00:14,568 --> 00:00:16,075
Now you want to get in trouble for gambling too?

6
00:00:16,075 --> 00:00:17,964
If you wanted to yell at me, you should’ve done that when—

7
00:00:17,964 --> 00:00:18,737
Are you hurt?

8
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:22,315
I’m not joking, P’Niran.

9
00:00:22,315 --> 00:00:23,371
I’m really worried about you.

10
00:00:23,371 --> 00:00:24,722
You’re my whole world.

11
00:00:24,722 --> 00:00:26,004
I’ll protect this world.

12
00:00:26,004 --> 00:00:26,912
So what did the teacher say?

13
00:00:26,912 --> 00:00:28,735
He asked me to pick up 100 pieces of trash.

14
00:00:28,735 --> 00:00:29,666
Right now?

15
00:00:29,666 --> 00:00:31,392
Well… what star am I like?

16
00:00:31,392 --> 00:00:32,252
The North Star.

17
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:34,188
I like the North Star more than anything in the world.

18
00:01:40,476 --> 00:01:41,504
Look at him.

19
00:01:41,769 --> 00:01:43,114
He’s probably floating off into space.

20
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:45,875
Do you miss Nong Cheewa, P’Niran?

21
00:01:46,874 --> 00:01:48,151
Nong, my ass.

22
00:01:48,518 --> 00:01:50,089
Why am I even on
the same color team as you?

23
00:01:50,293 --> 00:01:51,860
I would’ve signed up for judo to throw you.

24
00:01:52,390 --> 00:01:54,256
Asshole,
are you going to throw me every day?

25
00:01:54,664 --> 00:01:55,512
Enough already.

26
00:01:55,940 --> 00:01:57,051
If not “Nong”,

27
00:01:57,051 --> 00:01:59,180
then what should we call him, P’Niran?

28
00:02:00,608 --> 00:02:02,984
You guys are talking nonsense.

29
00:02:03,555 --> 00:02:04,197
By the way,

30
00:02:04,421 --> 00:02:08,543
what color team are
Cheewa, Jomyut, and Newton on?

31
00:02:08,829 --> 00:02:09,538
The Blue team.

32
00:02:11,169 --> 00:02:12,189
How do you know?

33
00:02:13,360 --> 00:02:14,045
Well…

34
00:02:16,044 --> 00:02:17,092
Don’t you have to leave early today?

35
00:02:19,111 --> 00:02:20,751
We’ve only ever gone home together.

36
00:02:21,567 --> 00:02:23,506
I want to go to school with you for a change.

37
00:02:25,790 --> 00:02:27,333
You can’t walk with me, kid.

38
00:02:27,884 --> 00:02:30,142
Our color teams are direct rivals.

39
00:02:35,648 --> 00:02:36,916
Hey, I’m just kidding.

40
00:02:39,812 --> 00:02:40,962
Did you know?

41
00:02:41,227 --> 00:02:42,955
You're an early Gemini.

42
00:02:42,955 --> 00:02:44,225
I'm a late Gemini.

43
00:02:44,511 --> 00:02:45,886
We're not that far apart in age.

44
00:02:46,477 --> 00:02:48,245
You don’t have to call me “Nong” anymore.

45
00:02:49,774 --> 00:02:51,232
If you don’t want me to call you “Nong,”

46
00:02:52,170 --> 00:02:53,225
then what should I call you?

47
00:02:55,509 --> 00:02:56,854
How about…

48
00:02:57,853 --> 00:02:59,000
“Little one”?

49
00:02:59,775 --> 00:03:00,380
Hmm?

50
00:03:01,073 --> 00:03:02,571
Little one.

51
00:03:07,451 --> 00:03:08,299
Little one.

52
00:03:10,726 --> 00:03:12,284
P’Cheewin told me

53
00:03:12,427 --> 00:03:14,183
he calls his partner “little one.”

54
00:03:14,713 --> 00:03:17,243
Do you really want to call me that, P’Niran?

55
00:03:20,445 --> 00:03:22,193
I don’t know. Just call me whatever you want.

56
00:03:22,397 --> 00:03:24,086
How about you call me Mr.?

57
00:03:26,492 --> 00:03:27,987
Young Master Niran, did you know?

58
00:03:27,987 --> 00:03:29,640
Oh, come on.

59
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:32,481
Why can’t you tell
when I’m joking or being serious?

60
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:33,373
Let’s go.

61
00:03:33,924 --> 00:03:37,460
I don’t want your student council
or your president’s gang scolding me.

62
00:03:41,416 --> 00:03:42,983
So observant.

63
00:03:43,452 --> 00:03:46,122
Well, well, well!

64
00:03:46,122 --> 00:03:47,402
Shut up, guys.

65
00:03:47,783 --> 00:03:48,740
I think he’s really down bad.

66
00:03:49,575 --> 00:03:51,868
Hey, are we competing in any sports?

67
00:03:53,255 --> 00:03:54,280
Sports again?

68
00:03:54,545 --> 00:03:55,655
We did that last year.

69
00:03:55,777 --> 00:03:56,817
You really want to do it again this year?

70
00:03:57,225 --> 00:03:59,182
Can I use the seniors’ quota to skip it?

71
00:03:59,447 --> 00:04:00,135
Yeah.

72
00:04:00,482 --> 00:04:01,736
I don’t think I’m competing this year.

73
00:04:01,736 --> 00:04:02,573
I’m lazy.

74
00:04:02,675 --> 00:04:04,055
What about you, Niran?

75
00:04:04,218 --> 00:04:05,276
Are you doing any sports?

76
00:04:08,131 --> 00:04:11,453
Even if you don’t sign up,
your team will come begging you to.

77
00:04:12,085 --> 00:04:14,251
Niran.

78
00:04:14,251 --> 00:04:17,172
So lucky
we’re on the same color team again.

79
00:04:17,804 --> 00:04:18,992
Do you want to play any sports this year?

80
00:04:19,645 --> 00:04:20,720
See? I was spot on.

81
00:04:20,878 --> 00:04:22,299
Call me Master Hem.

82
00:04:22,299 --> 00:04:23,381
Hello, Master.

83
00:04:23,891 --> 00:04:25,331
Do I really have to this year?

84
00:04:25,331 --> 00:04:26,651
I’m in Grade 12 already. Can I skip it?

85
00:04:26,855 --> 00:04:27,989
Let the juniors play.

86
00:04:27,989 --> 00:04:30,387
The juniors are begging for you.

87
00:04:30,387 --> 00:04:32,886
They all want their P’Niran to compete.

88
00:04:32,886 --> 00:04:33,761
Mm.

89
00:04:34,480 --> 00:04:37,160
Please. Just compete in something.

90
00:04:38,297 --> 00:04:39,292
Alright then.

91
00:04:40,454 --> 00:04:41,164
Let me sign you up.

92
00:04:42,473 --> 00:04:43,226
Niran.

93
00:04:53,779 --> 00:04:55,493
Mr. Niran, are you looking for me?

94
00:04:57,920 --> 00:04:59,588
Mr.? Don’t call me that.

95
00:04:59,588 --> 00:05:00,890
It sounds so distant.

96
00:05:02,032 --> 00:05:02,738
Alright.

97
00:05:03,941 --> 00:05:05,660
You don’t like us being distant.

98
00:05:07,373 --> 00:05:08,338
My heart is full now.

99
00:05:11,523 --> 00:05:12,444
What’s he talking about?

100
00:05:22,396 --> 00:05:23,282
Are you sleepy?

101
00:05:25,362 --> 00:05:26,979
Well, I don’t have classes.

102
00:05:26,979 --> 00:05:28,546
And the others are busy with their activities.

103
00:05:29,402 --> 00:05:30,263
So yeah, a little.

104
00:05:31,058 --> 00:05:32,952
Seniors have it the easiest, huh?

105
00:05:34,971 --> 00:05:35,895
How?

106
00:05:36,262 --> 00:05:37,339
I don’t have it easy at all.

107
00:05:39,786 --> 00:05:43,661
P’Niran, did you know
why dinosaurs became extinct?

108
00:05:46,475 --> 00:05:47,531
Because an asteroid hit Earth?

109
00:05:48,265 --> 00:05:49,030
Wrong.

110
00:05:49,927 --> 00:05:54,953
Because on a meteor shower night,
a dinosaur made a wish on that shooting star

111
00:05:55,218 --> 00:05:57,451
that it wanted 10,000 more wishes.

112
00:05:57,614 --> 00:05:58,610
After that,

113
00:05:58,773 --> 00:06:01,347
10,000 more meteors
came crashing down on Earth.

114
00:06:01,653 --> 00:06:03,387
Hmm…

115
00:06:03,680 --> 00:06:04,897
Funny, right?

116
00:06:05,346 --> 00:06:06,952
I know you like cracking jokes.

117
00:06:06,952 --> 00:06:08,859
So I did the math.

118
00:06:08,920 --> 00:06:11,725
Out of the 48 jokes I came up with,

119
00:06:11,725 --> 00:06:13,707
I figured you’d like this one the most.

120
00:06:16,745 --> 00:06:18,313
That’s great.

121
00:06:18,313 --> 00:06:19,636
Do you want to hear some more?

122
00:06:19,636 --> 00:06:20,556
I wrote them all down.

123
00:06:21,820 --> 00:06:23,109
No, I’m good.

124
00:06:23,435 --> 00:06:25,484
And please don’t say that to anyone else.

125
00:06:25,484 --> 00:06:26,282
Or they might copy your line.

126
00:06:29,259 --> 00:06:30,963
What are you doing here?

127
00:06:32,268 --> 00:06:33,506
My friends asked me to buy stuff for them.

128
00:06:34,118 --> 00:06:34,917
Wanna help me?

129
00:06:35,651 --> 00:06:36,435
Of course.

130
00:06:40,452 --> 00:06:42,289
Where are Jomyut and Newton?
I haven’t seen them.

131
00:06:42,738 --> 00:06:46,549
They’re at the club, working on
an upgraded version of the alien detector.

132
00:06:46,936 --> 00:06:47,644
Again?

133
00:06:48,235 --> 00:06:49,359
Haven’t they learned?

134
00:06:49,991 --> 00:06:51,501
The janitor’s going to
chase them down the building again.

135
00:06:52,684 --> 00:06:54,121
Are you sure you don’t want me
to help you carry those?

136
00:06:54,386 --> 00:06:55,031
They’re light as a feather.

137
00:06:55,765 --> 00:06:57,335
But you asked for my help.

138
00:07:01,240 --> 00:07:02,861
I didn’t ask you to help carry them.

139
00:07:03,860 --> 00:07:06,805
I just wanted you to keep me company.

140
00:07:07,763 --> 00:07:08,456
Can’t you do that?

141
00:07:17,478 --> 00:07:18,730
Cheewa, watch out!

142
00:07:19,831 --> 00:07:20,536
Cheewa!

143
00:07:25,430 --> 00:07:27,206
I’m so sorry again, Cheewa.

144
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:31,392
It’s normal.

145
00:07:31,657 --> 00:07:36,143
When an object like a ball
weighing approximately 450 grams

146
00:07:36,143 --> 00:07:38,712
comes hurtling at 30 kilometers per hour
or more,

147
00:07:38,712 --> 00:07:42,065
the impact can cause a nosebleed
and blurred vision.

148
00:07:43,758 --> 00:07:44,451
Cheewa.

149
00:07:46,246 --> 00:07:47,349
Your glasses are broken.

150
00:07:48,756 --> 00:07:49,945
You’re bleeding too.

151
00:07:50,088 --> 00:07:51,536
Let’s go to the nurse’s office now.

152
00:07:52,923 --> 00:07:54,426
Are you okay? Are you still dizzy?

153
00:07:55,792 --> 00:07:57,197
It’s really bad.

154
00:07:59,726 --> 00:08:01,986
The snacks! I forgot the snacks!

155
00:08:06,921 --> 00:08:08,215
Without your glasses,

156
00:08:08,439 --> 00:08:09,823
you look pretty handsome.

157
00:08:10,272 --> 00:08:11,758
A bit less handsome than me.

158
00:08:12,717 --> 00:08:13,842
How nearsighted are you?

159
00:08:14,883 --> 00:08:16,286
Almost -10.

160
00:08:18,223 --> 00:08:20,285
That must make your life really difficult.

161
00:08:20,652 --> 00:08:22,098
Not that difficult.

162
00:08:23,179 --> 00:08:24,264
Drink some water.

163
00:08:26,528 --> 00:08:27,975
Hey, hey, hey!

164
00:08:28,403 --> 00:08:29,472
I think it does make it difficult.

165
00:08:29,901 --> 00:08:30,669
Yeah.

166
00:08:31,138 --> 00:08:32,147
My mom is only -4,

167
00:08:32,147 --> 00:08:34,000
and she’s already complaining that
she can’t find the remote in her hand.

168
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:34,955
What are you going to do?

169
00:08:35,546 --> 00:08:36,595
Do you have a spare pair?

170
00:08:36,982 --> 00:08:39,107
Do we need to call P’Cheewin to bring them?

171
00:08:40,045 --> 00:08:41,357
I don’t have a spare pair.

172
00:08:41,357 --> 00:08:42,342
Well then.

173
00:08:46,013 --> 00:08:47,837
Please take care of him, P’Niran.

174
00:08:48,367 --> 00:08:50,938
Just stick to P’Niran like toffee, kid.

175
00:08:51,774 --> 00:08:53,432
You better have your glasses ready tomorrow.

176
00:08:53,636 --> 00:08:55,312
P’Niran has a judo match.

177
00:08:55,496 --> 00:08:56,659
Every year on Sports Day,

178
00:08:56,659 --> 00:08:58,790
the school president is pretty busy

179
00:08:59,381 --> 00:09:02,402
taking care of all the color teams,

180
00:09:03,320 --> 00:09:05,508
but I’ll make sure to be there for you, P’Niran.

181
00:09:07,058 --> 00:09:09,605
Ooooh!

182
00:09:11,787 --> 00:09:13,102
You guys are crazy.

183
00:09:14,999 --> 00:09:16,363
Get it together.

184
00:09:18,831 --> 00:09:20,885
Alright, drink some water.
I’ve been holding it for a while.

185
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:25,354
What’s toffee?

186
00:09:25,354 --> 00:09:26,234
No idea.

187
00:09:26,234 --> 00:09:27,449
It’s a candy.

188
00:09:27,449 --> 00:09:28,463
You know, the kind that comes on a stick.

189
00:09:28,463 --> 00:09:29,440
Why does it stick together?

190
00:09:29,440 --> 00:09:30,972
I heard it’s sticky.

191
00:09:34,721 --> 00:09:45,052
RED TEAM

192
00:09:45,052 --> 00:09:45,949
Hey, kid.

193
00:09:45,949 --> 00:09:47,159
Do you want to go back to your Blue team?

194
00:09:48,892 --> 00:09:49,616
Huh?

195
00:09:50,187 --> 00:09:52,022
Do you want to go back to your Blue team?

196
00:09:54,449 --> 00:09:55,116
Open your mouth.

197
00:09:57,257 --> 00:09:58,134
Ouch!

198
00:09:59,867 --> 00:10:00,892
I’m sorry.

199
00:10:01,565 --> 00:10:03,290
You’re supposed to eat the snack,
not my fingers.

200
00:10:03,657 --> 00:10:05,333
Is the snack sweet, buddy?

201
00:10:05,760 --> 00:10:07,160
You’re snacking with him.

202
00:10:07,160 --> 00:10:08,619
How could you be lonely?

203
00:10:08,905 --> 00:10:09,973
Don’t bite my fingers.

204
00:10:09,973 --> 00:10:11,292
To the left.

205
00:10:11,741 --> 00:10:12,721
My left.

206
00:10:12,925 --> 00:10:14,285
Stay still. I’ll put it in.

207
00:10:14,285 --> 00:10:15,218
Good job.

208
00:10:15,789 --> 00:10:16,996
I’ll give you a reward.

209
00:10:17,669 --> 00:10:19,113
Turn around three times.

210
00:10:19,847 --> 00:10:20,598
Yeah.

211
00:10:20,802 --> 00:10:21,694
You’re so easy to take care of.

212
00:10:22,551 --> 00:10:24,251
GO, RED TEAM!
Ah!

213
00:10:24,251 --> 00:10:25,682
Who were you feeding just now?

214
00:10:25,682 --> 00:10:26,654
P’Niran, of course.

215
00:10:26,654 --> 00:10:27,299
Really?

216
00:10:27,768 --> 00:10:28,865
Now, feed yourself.

217
00:10:28,865 --> 00:10:29,515
One more time.

218
00:10:29,515 --> 00:10:30,797
Feed yourself.

219
00:10:31,021 --> 00:10:31,843
Feed yourself.

220
00:10:32,047 --> 00:10:33,735
Make it funny.

221
00:10:35,122 --> 00:10:36,969
This isn’t funny. No one’s behind you.

222
00:10:36,969 --> 00:10:38,631
Feed yourself.

223
00:10:47,382 --> 00:10:48,757
You really can’t see?

224
00:10:51,388 --> 00:10:52,120
It’s here.

225
00:10:56,443 --> 00:10:57,167
Yeah.

226
00:10:57,668 --> 00:10:58,680
Shake them off too.

227
00:10:59,530 --> 00:11:00,614
Watch your head.

228
00:11:10,506 --> 00:11:12,298
Now that I get a good look at you,

229
00:11:13,256 --> 00:11:14,303
you’re pretty handsome.

230
00:11:17,056 --> 00:11:18,830
Even though I can’t see very clearly,

231
00:11:20,115 --> 00:11:21,568
I can hear you.

232
00:11:34,211 --> 00:11:34,955
What’s wrong?

233
00:11:36,566 --> 00:11:38,569
I get shy too, you know?

234
00:11:46,013 --> 00:11:46,664
Mm.

235
00:11:47,500 --> 00:11:48,117
Can we go now?

236
00:11:52,207 --> 00:11:52,952
Can you see?

237
00:11:54,930 --> 00:11:55,893
Not really.

238
00:11:56,260 --> 00:11:57,582
Hold onto my shirt then.

239
00:11:58,235 --> 00:11:59,326
Hold onto my arm.

240
00:12:02,854 --> 00:12:03,811
Can you walk okay?

241
00:12:04,321 --> 00:12:05,710
Can I ride on your back?

242
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:06,960
Don’t be ridiculous.

243
00:12:07,164 --> 00:12:08,151
I’m sorry.

244
00:12:10,578 --> 00:12:11,898
I can’t really see.

245
00:12:12,428 --> 00:12:14,075
That’s pretty bad.

246
00:12:18,522 --> 00:12:19,237
Here.

247
00:12:21,236 --> 00:12:23,719
No. Whoa, it’s really bad.

248
00:12:26,411 --> 00:12:27,434
I got this from the science room.

249
00:12:28,331 --> 00:12:29,617
I thought you might find it useful.

250
00:12:31,289 --> 00:12:32,042
Is that okay?

251
00:12:32,593 --> 00:12:33,317
Does it help?

252
00:12:34,826 --> 00:12:35,946
You have such doe eyes.

253
00:12:37,088 --> 00:12:39,873
I feel so much better
now that I can see you up close.

254
00:12:40,485 --> 00:12:41,570
Yeah, just do whatever you want.

255
00:12:42,345 --> 00:12:43,823
You actually look like an alien.

256
00:12:43,945 --> 00:12:44,872
Are you an alien?

257
00:12:48,280 --> 00:12:49,012
Huh?

258
00:12:49,216 --> 00:12:50,269
You looked through it and drank the water?

259
00:12:50,269 --> 00:12:51,284
There!

260
00:12:51,590 --> 00:12:52,275
Hey.

261
00:12:52,640 --> 00:12:53,759
What a mess.

262
00:13:04,110 --> 00:13:05,334
Hold my hand

263
00:13:05,702 --> 00:13:07,017
so you don’t trip getting on the bus.

264
00:13:10,565 --> 00:13:12,042
Hold my shoulders.

265
00:13:24,105 --> 00:13:25,450
M.W.B.

266
00:13:27,888 --> 00:13:28,895
I don’t think we’re getting any seats.

267
00:13:31,182 --> 00:13:32,295
We can stand.

268
00:13:32,530 --> 00:13:33,216
Are you sure?

269
00:13:37,924 --> 00:13:39,182
Hold my hand

270
00:13:39,518 --> 00:13:40,935
so you don’t trip getting on the bus.

271
00:13:57,330 --> 00:13:58,292
Are you okay?

272
00:13:59,436 --> 00:14:00,776
It’s harder than I thought.

273
00:14:01,936 --> 00:14:02,806
Here, stand like this.

274
00:14:07,901 --> 00:14:08,912
Hold my shoulders.

275
00:14:11,300 --> 00:14:12,195
Is this okay?

276
00:14:13,036 --> 00:14:13,691
Yes.

277
00:14:15,238 --> 00:14:16,728
P’Niran, did you know that

278
00:14:17,754 --> 00:14:19,510
from where we stand,

279
00:14:20,048 --> 00:14:21,867
if the driver brakes,

280
00:14:23,549 --> 00:14:26,684
gravity could make me hug you from behind?

281
00:14:27,861 --> 00:14:28,989
What is it now?

282
00:14:30,334 --> 00:14:31,314
Stop talking.

283
00:14:32,424 --> 00:14:33,241
Hold on properly.

284
00:14:40,398 --> 00:14:41,703
I said, hold on properly.

285
00:14:41,970 --> 00:14:42,470
Okay.

286
00:14:43,244 --> 00:14:45,046
Hold on properly!

287
00:14:47,468 --> 00:14:48,865
What kind of driving is that?

288
00:14:49,151 --> 00:14:50,628
Gosh!

289
00:15:12,951 --> 00:15:13,787
We’ve arrived.

290
00:15:16,377 --> 00:15:17,131
Is this it?

291
00:15:19,216 --> 00:15:19,954
By the way,

292
00:15:21,097 --> 00:15:24,865
I’ve never walked you home before,
even though we live so close.

293
00:15:26,681 --> 00:15:27,712
Nice house.

294
00:15:28,486 --> 00:15:29,718
Not really.

295
00:15:32,752 --> 00:15:34,414
Do you need me to walk you inside?

296
00:15:34,700 --> 00:15:36,144
Or can you manage?

297
00:15:36,144 --> 00:15:37,188
Do you want to come inside?

298
00:15:37,843 --> 00:15:39,222
No, it’s fine.

299
00:15:39,626 --> 00:15:40,682
See you tomorrow.

300
00:15:41,018 --> 00:15:41,660
Okay.

301
00:15:43,641 --> 00:15:44,691
P’Niran.

302
00:15:47,482 --> 00:15:48,552
Good luck tomorrow.

303
00:15:51,394 --> 00:15:52,684
I’m competing against the Blue team.

304
00:15:52,970 --> 00:15:55,817
Are you sure you want to
cheer for your opponent?

305
00:16:05,620 --> 00:16:06,328
Damn.

306
00:16:06,917 --> 00:16:07,768
I’m excited.

307
00:16:07,768 --> 00:16:09,637
I haven’t seen this vibe in so long.

308
00:16:10,064 --> 00:16:11,916
Thipok, why aren’t you on the drums?

309
00:16:11,916 --> 00:16:12,887
Hype your friends up.

310
00:16:13,139 --> 00:16:14,720
Cheering is more fun.

311
00:16:14,838 --> 00:16:16,870
Let the juniors take care of that.

312
00:16:17,627 --> 00:16:19,460
Who do you think Cheewa is rooting for?

313
00:16:20,587 --> 00:16:22,073
One of them is from his team.

314
00:16:22,628 --> 00:16:23,924
The other is his opponent,

315
00:16:24,613 --> 00:16:26,097
but the owner of his heart.

316
00:16:26,272 --> 00:16:27,793
If Niran hears you say that,

317
00:16:27,793 --> 00:16:29,047
he’s going to throw you.

318
00:16:29,047 --> 00:16:32,056
Wait, but Cheewa said
he’d come to cheer him on, didn’t he?

319
00:16:32,762 --> 00:16:33,477
I haven’t seen him.

320
00:16:33,792 --> 00:16:36,900
Honestly, I don’t think
the president’s crew would have the time.

321
00:16:43,883 --> 00:16:45,086
There he is!

322
00:16:45,086 --> 00:16:47,632
Woo!

323
00:16:47,632 --> 00:16:48,482
Woo!

324
00:16:48,792 --> 00:16:51,014
Go, Niran!

325
00:16:51,975 --> 00:16:53,429
It doesn’t matter how much cheer you get.

326
00:16:53,429 --> 00:16:55,632
What matters is if the person you like
shows up to cheer for you.

327
00:16:56,439 --> 00:16:58,059
You’re freaking distracting him.

328
00:16:58,311 --> 00:16:59,726
Stop it, Hem.

329
00:17:00,113 --> 00:17:03,381
Athletes from both teams,
please exchange bows!

330
00:17:03,792 --> 00:17:06,918
May I also ask both cheering squads
to quiet down?

331
00:17:07,153 --> 00:17:08,415
Our athletes need to focus.

332
00:17:26,860 --> 00:17:27,737
Begin!

333
00:17:48,691 --> 00:17:49,780
I’m competing against the Blue team.

334
00:17:50,536 --> 00:17:53,392
Are you sure you want to
cheer for your opponent?

335
00:17:54,569 --> 00:17:56,325
Sports Day won't affect my grades.

336
00:17:57,536 --> 00:18:00,088
Of course I'm going to
cheer for my crush’s team.

337
00:18:03,266 --> 00:18:05,182
Fine. Just make sure
you get there in time to cheer.

338
00:18:23,041 --> 00:18:24,064
It’s okay.

339
00:18:24,893 --> 00:18:26,359
You can still try for third place.

340
00:18:26,359 --> 00:18:27,267
What’s wrong?

341
00:18:27,452 --> 00:18:29,037
You looked completely distracted
during the match.

342
00:18:29,659 --> 00:18:31,695
You don't usually lose your edge this easily.

343
00:18:34,570 --> 00:18:36,115
He was really distracted

344
00:18:36,821 --> 00:18:39,300
because someone from the Blue team
came to sit on our side.

345
00:18:40,813 --> 00:18:42,506
You’re running your mouth again, P’Hem.

346
00:18:42,872 --> 00:18:43,905
Don’t blame my friend.

347
00:18:44,040 --> 00:18:46,360
Oh, hey, Jom, my dear bro.

348
00:18:46,595 --> 00:18:48,248
I haven’t really seen you around lately.

349
00:18:48,483 --> 00:18:53,512
I, Newton, and the other members
are working on a top-secret alien exploration mission.

350
00:18:53,512 --> 00:18:55,048
We’re not sitting around doing nothing
like you guys.

351
00:18:57,638 --> 00:18:59,538
Yeah, it’s really top secret.

352
00:18:59,538 --> 00:19:00,484
No one knows about it.

353
00:19:01,190 --> 00:19:01,923
Yeah.

354
00:19:03,201 --> 00:19:04,020
Come on.

355
00:19:06,596 --> 00:19:07,861
Ouch!

356
00:19:13,023 --> 00:19:13,813
Here’s some water.

357
00:19:17,580 --> 00:19:18,352
Thanks.

358
00:19:21,913 --> 00:19:23,273
Would you like anything else to eat?

359
00:19:23,609 --> 00:19:25,792
All of us are here
and you only bought one bottle?

360
00:19:25,792 --> 00:19:27,546
Let’s go grab some cold water.

361
00:19:27,681 --> 00:19:28,594
I’m thirsty too.

362
00:19:29,428 --> 00:19:30,045
Come on.

363
00:19:30,886 --> 00:19:32,134
We don’t have anyone to buy it for us.

364
00:19:32,134 --> 00:19:34,136
There’s a whole group of us
and he only got one bottle.

365
00:19:34,657 --> 00:19:36,007
What are you waiting for? Let’s go.

366
00:19:43,792 --> 00:19:44,731
Are you feeling better?

367
00:19:47,573 --> 00:19:48,866
I just lost a Sports Day match.

368
00:19:49,084 --> 00:19:50,026
You don’t have to comfort me.

369
00:19:51,169 --> 00:19:54,250
I thought you said Sports Day
doesn’t have anything to do with grades.

370
00:20:01,770 --> 00:20:02,723
It’s okay.

371
00:20:05,867 --> 00:20:06,841
Free hugs.

372
00:20:19,589 --> 00:20:21,730
You're the best in my eyes, P’Niran.

373
00:20:22,739 --> 00:20:25,027
No matter how many times you lose,

374
00:20:26,992 --> 00:20:28,862
you'll always win my heart.

375
00:20:31,233 --> 00:20:32,062
Thanks.

376
00:20:32,466 --> 00:20:33,174
I’m touched.

377
00:20:36,470 --> 00:20:37,217
This is it.

378
00:20:38,226 --> 00:20:39,945
I’m definitely winning you over.

379
00:20:40,096 --> 00:20:41,742
Hmm…

380
00:20:48,952 --> 00:20:50,281
Are you going to let me hug you all night?

381
00:20:50,912 --> 00:20:52,377
I’m free tonight.

382
00:20:53,369 --> 00:20:54,809
Hmm…

383
00:20:54,809 --> 00:20:55,694
This kid.

384
00:20:58,199 --> 00:20:59,286
You little puppy.

385
00:21:08,535 --> 00:21:11,050
Damn. As soon as they heard
the Astronomy Club has AC on,

386
00:21:11,050 --> 00:21:12,818
they all came freeloading.

387
00:21:13,306 --> 00:21:15,063
You’re welcome to visit often, P’Niran.

388
00:21:16,190 --> 00:21:18,106
Yeah, I’m sensitive to AC, though.

389
00:21:19,048 --> 00:21:20,494
But I guess I could sneak in for a nap.

390
00:21:22,579 --> 00:21:24,031
I smelled it earlier when we hugged.

391
00:21:25,326 --> 00:21:26,375
Are you wearing perfume again?

392
00:21:30,831 --> 00:21:32,652
I just wanted to impress you.

393
00:21:33,056 --> 00:21:33,741
Do you like it?

394
00:21:40,952 --> 00:21:41,623
Why are you smiling?

395
00:21:42,346 --> 00:21:43,348
Stop smiling.

396
00:21:45,332 --> 00:21:46,257
Why not?

397
00:21:49,351 --> 00:21:50,074
Don’t smile.

398
00:21:53,118 --> 00:21:53,937
Sorry.

399
00:21:57,064 --> 00:21:58,384
I can’t stop smiling.

400
00:21:58,619 --> 00:21:59,888
Let me smile with my back turned.

401
00:22:06,479 --> 00:22:07,542
Watch out!

402
00:22:10,952 --> 00:22:11,586
Hi.

403
00:22:11,586 --> 00:22:12,611
Hi.

404
00:22:13,072 --> 00:22:14,607
Are you seriously not going to
get a single thing right?

405
00:22:15,111 --> 00:22:16,084
You don’t even care about studying.

406
00:22:17,076 --> 00:22:18,078
Please calm down.

407
00:22:30,507 --> 00:22:31,776
What the hell is it this time?

408
00:22:33,540 --> 00:22:35,584
Did you really think you’d scared me off
after messing with me last time?

409
00:22:36,034 --> 00:22:38,170
This time, you dressed as a ghost
to punch me.

410
00:22:38,771 --> 00:22:40,496
Asshole, what’s your problem with me?

411
00:22:40,496 --> 00:22:40,996
Why?

412
00:22:40,996 --> 00:22:41,890
- What do you want?
- What are you gonna do?

413
00:22:41,890 --> 00:22:42,846
Please don’t, P’Niran.

414
00:22:46,656 --> 00:22:48,349
You jerk keep accusing people
with no evidence.

415
00:22:48,518 --> 00:22:49,658
You’re hilarious, you know that?

416
00:22:49,921 --> 00:22:50,943
Where were you an hour ago?

417
00:22:50,943 --> 00:22:51,810
I was in a judo match.

418
00:22:51,810 --> 00:22:52,687
There were like 10 witnesses.

419
00:22:52,687 --> 00:22:53,434
Don’t be stupid.

420
00:22:53,434 --> 00:22:54,313
I don’t believe you.

421
00:22:54,482 --> 00:22:55,428
Go get some evidence.

422
00:22:55,991 --> 00:22:57,055
You’re asking for evidence?

423
00:22:57,149 --> 00:22:58,264
Now you’re asking for evidence?

424
00:22:58,264 --> 00:23:00,007
Why didn’t you ask before
you pushed me and punched me earlier?

425
00:23:00,232 --> 00:23:01,074
All you deserve

426
00:23:01,074 --> 00:23:02,549
is a beating!

427
00:23:02,549 --> 00:23:03,952
- Bring it. What the hell is wrong with you?
- No, P’Niran.

428
00:23:04,590 --> 00:23:05,835
You don’t want to be put on probation.

429
00:23:06,642 --> 00:23:09,383
This time, you could actually get suspended.

430
00:23:19,381 --> 00:23:20,717
You shouldn’t have stopped me earlier.

431
00:23:24,602 --> 00:23:25,692
Please calm down.

432
00:23:27,325 --> 00:23:28,518
Damn, this is so frustrating.

433
00:23:31,634 --> 00:23:34,636
On a scale of 1 to 10,
how mad were you at the time?

434
00:23:38,634 --> 00:23:39,487
I don’t know.

435
00:23:41,007 --> 00:23:42,345
Did you know?

436
00:23:44,863 --> 00:23:46,327
I want you to try this.

437
00:23:47,341 --> 00:23:49,535
When you’re angry, tell yourself

438
00:23:50,248 --> 00:23:54,174
your amygdala is at an 8 out of 10
on the anger scale.

439
00:23:55,356 --> 00:23:56,814
Scientifically speaking,

440
00:23:57,940 --> 00:24:00,737
if we mention the part of our brain
that controls our emotions,

441
00:24:01,244 --> 00:24:02,907
it helps us calm down.

442
00:24:04,014 --> 00:24:06,564
Because that switch gets turned off
when we’re angry.

443
00:24:09,661 --> 00:24:10,939
Who would be as calm as you?

444
00:24:10,939 --> 00:24:12,181
I’m not calm.

445
00:24:13,082 --> 00:24:14,972
Earlier, I was 9/10 mad

446
00:24:14,972 --> 00:24:16,615
when he pushed you.

447
00:24:17,572 --> 00:24:19,136
This method helped me.

448
00:24:29,600 --> 00:24:30,595
Did you lose a Sports Day match today?

449
00:24:36,451 --> 00:24:38,723
It wasn’t that serious.

450
00:24:39,511 --> 00:24:43,530
I’ve been following Coach Ong’s
new schedule for me.

451
00:24:46,458 --> 00:24:47,183
Why?

452
00:24:47,596 --> 00:24:49,253
What did he call to tell you this time?

453
00:24:49,535 --> 00:24:51,573
Don’t blame your coach or anyone else.

454
00:24:53,731 --> 00:24:54,655
I saw it myself.

455
00:24:54,943 --> 00:24:55,558
Huh?

456
00:24:56,422 --> 00:24:57,722
You went to watch me at school?

457
00:24:58,529 --> 00:24:59,191
Yes.

458
00:24:59,943 --> 00:25:00,979
You didn’t tell me.

459
00:25:01,310 --> 00:25:02,714
I didn’t want to distract you.

460
00:25:04,783 --> 00:25:06,815
But when I saw you lose, I couldn’t stand it.

461
00:25:23,214 --> 00:25:24,412
I don’t want to do it anymore.

462
00:25:29,136 --> 00:25:33,726
Do you realize that
even your grades are dropping?

463
00:25:36,560 --> 00:25:37,820
What have you been doing lately?

464
00:25:39,265 --> 00:25:39,778
Huh?

465
00:25:42,255 --> 00:25:43,797
Are you seriously not going to
get a single thing right?

466
00:25:44,961 --> 00:25:45,974
You don’t even care about studying.

467
00:25:48,414 --> 00:25:49,651
Can we not talk about this?

468
00:25:57,490 --> 00:25:58,940
Tell me honestly.

469
00:26:00,948 --> 00:26:03,765
Without judo, what would you be?

470
00:26:13,200 --> 00:26:14,481
You keep asking stuff like this.

471
00:26:16,114 --> 00:26:19,705
Have you ever asked me if I really liked it?

472
00:26:20,193 --> 00:26:21,421
I mean, it makes no sense.

473
00:26:22,622 --> 00:26:30,228
How do you go from being a national athlete
to an incompetent slacker like this?

474
00:26:38,686 --> 00:26:40,121
What’s a competent person like, Dad?

475
00:26:42,617 --> 00:26:43,858
Is it someone like you

476
00:26:44,783 --> 00:26:47,132
who’s the reason
Mom has been gone from us all this time?

477
00:26:47,770 --> 00:26:48,525
Niran.

478
00:26:50,852 --> 00:26:52,160
I’ve always thought

479
00:26:53,793 --> 00:26:55,205
I wanted Mom to come back to us.

480
00:26:57,495 --> 00:27:01,177
But you keep destroying that belief.

481
00:27:03,148 --> 00:27:04,271
You know why?

482
00:27:06,730 --> 00:27:08,793
Because I don’t even freaking want
to live here myself!

483
00:27:08,924 --> 00:27:09,546
Right here!

484
00:27:09,546 --> 00:27:10,239
With you!

485
00:27:13,280 --> 00:27:14,634
If you’re so tough, go get your mom back.

486
00:27:23,459 --> 00:27:24,586
Mom loves me.

487
00:27:27,207 --> 00:27:29,665
I could follow her.

488
00:27:31,767 --> 00:27:33,182
She’d be waiting for me anyway.

489
00:28:01,079 --> 00:28:01,767
Hi, Mom.

490
00:28:01,767 --> 00:28:02,762
(Hello, Niran.)

491
00:28:03,475 --> 00:28:04,748
(This weekend,)

492
00:28:04,748 --> 00:28:06,518
(do you want to
grab something to eat with me?)

493
00:28:06,518 --> 00:28:07,359
Of course.

494
00:28:07,565 --> 00:28:09,364
I was literally just thinking of you.

495
00:28:09,364 --> 00:28:10,445
I want to see you so much.

496
00:28:12,303 --> 00:28:15,680
I’ve decided on something
and want to tell you about it.

497
00:28:15,680 --> 00:28:16,678
(Oh, really?)

498
00:28:16,678 --> 00:28:17,811
(Good.)

499
00:28:17,905 --> 00:28:19,162
(We can talk about it.)

500
00:28:19,612 --> 00:28:20,745
(See you soon.)

501
00:28:20,895 --> 00:28:22,273
(I miss you, son.)

502
00:28:22,273 --> 00:28:23,199
(Bye-bye.)

503
00:28:33,365 --> 00:28:34,211
Are you nervous?

504
00:28:35,578 --> 00:28:36,349
A little bit.

505
00:28:39,277 --> 00:28:40,011
Oh.

506
00:28:40,583 --> 00:28:41,842
Hey, Niran.

507
00:28:43,193 --> 00:28:45,036
- Hi.
- Hi.

508
00:28:45,411 --> 00:28:46,190
Have a seat.

509
00:28:46,509 --> 00:28:47,392
Thank you.

510
00:28:55,109 --> 00:28:56,728
How have you been?

511
00:28:57,723 --> 00:28:59,046
So-so.

512
00:28:59,403 --> 00:29:00,770
Nothing much.

513
00:29:02,140 --> 00:29:03,120
What about you, Mom?

514
00:29:03,402 --> 00:29:05,255
You invited me to eat out.

515
00:29:05,255 --> 00:29:06,356
Is there something you want to tell me?

516
00:29:06,976 --> 00:29:09,117
You usually visit me at home.

517
00:29:09,303 --> 00:29:12,555
We don’t get to see each other very often,

518
00:29:12,705 --> 00:29:15,878
so I wanted to bring you here
for some good food.

519
00:29:17,943 --> 00:29:19,164
How’s school?

520
00:29:19,539 --> 00:29:22,017
Have you thought about
what you want to study next?

521
00:29:23,556 --> 00:29:24,869
Not yet.

522
00:29:27,084 --> 00:29:27,882
Hey, Niran.

523
00:29:28,126 --> 00:29:30,554
I heard you’re into sports, right?

524
00:29:30,723 --> 00:29:31,428
Yes.

525
00:29:31,540 --> 00:29:33,273
I’m mainly doing judo now.

526
00:29:33,498 --> 00:29:34,239
Wow.

527
00:29:34,239 --> 00:29:35,261
You’re amazing.

528
00:29:35,903 --> 00:29:37,991
Let’s eat first.

529
00:29:37,991 --> 00:29:39,297
We can talk more later.

530
00:29:41,099 --> 00:29:41,809
Okay.

531
00:29:42,353 --> 00:29:43,101
Let’s begin.

532
00:29:43,101 --> 00:29:44,291
Here.

533
00:29:44,914 --> 00:29:46,381
Eat up.

534
00:29:46,381 --> 00:29:48,374
I ordered that for you.

535
00:29:48,374 --> 00:29:49,300
Thank you.

536
00:29:49,300 --> 00:29:50,156
Try this.

537
00:29:52,277 --> 00:29:54,156
Aww, thank you.

538
00:29:54,156 --> 00:29:56,542
You’re giving this to me first?
You’re not going to eat first?

539
00:29:57,330 --> 00:29:59,329
Have some too, Niran.

540
00:29:59,892 --> 00:30:03,153
I heard about your judo ranking, Niran.

541
00:30:03,866 --> 00:30:04,565
Yeah.

542
00:30:07,043 --> 00:30:09,127
Dad seems very disappointed in me.

543
00:30:11,154 --> 00:30:12,616
Are you disappointed in me?

544
00:30:13,348 --> 00:30:14,557
Not at all.

545
00:30:15,120 --> 00:30:17,463
I’ve never been disappointed in you.

546
00:30:18,120 --> 00:30:21,177
No matter what your judo ranking is,

547
00:30:21,515 --> 00:30:23,694
I’ll always be proud of you.

548
00:30:25,364 --> 00:30:26,791
I’m serious.

549
00:30:27,467 --> 00:30:28,453
I mean it.

550
00:30:29,617 --> 00:30:30,738
Thank you, Mom.

551
00:30:31,958 --> 00:30:33,936
I’ll always be rooting for you too, Niran.

552
00:30:34,255 --> 00:30:36,068
Don’t put too much pressure on yourself.

553
00:30:36,312 --> 00:30:40,113
Next time you have a match, let me know.

554
00:30:40,226 --> 00:30:41,606
I want to go cheer you on.

555
00:30:43,051 --> 00:30:43,718
Mm.

556
00:30:44,056 --> 00:30:45,644
And about your further studies,

557
00:30:46,057 --> 00:30:47,773
there’s no need to pressure yourself.

558
00:30:47,773 --> 00:30:50,286
If you can’t figure it out yet,
don’t force yourself.

559
00:30:51,224 --> 00:30:53,641
You can go to university anytime, right?

560
00:30:55,781 --> 00:30:56,579
Yes, Mom.

561
00:30:57,067 --> 00:30:59,697
Once I figure it out, you’ll be the first to know.

562
00:31:00,598 --> 00:31:03,341
I actually want you to
take me to apply to university.

563
00:31:04,783 --> 00:31:08,385
Who knows? I might move in with you too.

564
00:31:08,948 --> 00:31:11,178
If you have a spare room for me.

565
00:31:12,023 --> 00:31:13,747
Anytime.

566
00:31:21,633 --> 00:31:24,058
Niran, actually,

567
00:31:24,696 --> 00:31:28,918
there’s something
I want you to be the first to know.

568
00:31:42,473 --> 00:31:43,117
SON

569
00:31:51,038 --> 00:31:51,897
Thank you.

570
00:32:03,195 --> 00:32:05,691
Well, I’m…

571
00:32:07,943 --> 00:32:10,253
I’m getting married to Uncle Rit.

572
00:32:17,940 --> 00:32:20,888
But it’ll probably be a while
before the actual wedding.

573
00:32:24,585 --> 00:32:27,919
This is what I wanted you to know
before anyone else.

574
00:32:32,029 --> 00:32:35,142
Congratulations, Mom and Uncle Rit.

575
00:32:42,326 --> 00:32:43,945
I'll definitely be there.

576
00:32:44,208 --> 00:32:45,533
It’s your wedding, Mom.

577
00:32:45,533 --> 00:32:46,390
I wouldn’t miss it.

578
00:32:47,253 --> 00:32:49,629
I’ve never been to your wedding before.

579
00:33:03,717 --> 00:33:04,816
(One thing’s for sure.)

580
00:33:05,661 --> 00:33:09,346
(I can’t bring Mom back, just like Dad said.)

581
00:33:14,639 --> 00:33:17,278
(But will I get to live with her?)

582
00:33:22,383 --> 00:33:23,583
SON

583
00:33:23,752 --> 00:33:25,131
(I’m still not sure.)

584
00:33:28,172 --> 00:33:31,630
I just want my house to be
a place where you can do anything.

585
00:33:31,949 --> 00:33:33,352
You can cry and be sad.

586
00:33:34,065 --> 00:33:35,501
There’s no one to be embarrassed around.

587
00:33:36,402 --> 00:33:37,536
I’m here.

588
00:34:27,642 --> 00:34:28,445
What are you looking at?

589
00:34:28,445 --> 00:34:29,722
Haven’t you ever seen a 12th-grader cry?

590
00:34:32,028 --> 00:34:33,285
I’m here.

591
00:34:39,557 --> 00:34:40,794
Why did you have to show up now?

592
00:34:40,794 --> 00:34:41,760
This is so embarrassing.

593
00:34:43,593 --> 00:34:45,637
Just pretend I’m not here.

594
00:34:50,230 --> 00:34:51,517
How am I supposed to do that?

595
00:34:51,675 --> 00:34:52,710
You’re staring at me.

596
00:35:00,085 --> 00:35:03,115
You can wipe your tears with my shirt.

597
00:35:07,012 --> 00:35:08,083
Are you going to take it off?

598
00:35:09,916 --> 00:35:11,672
I’m wearing a vest underneath.

599
00:35:11,810 --> 00:35:12,580
It’s fine.

600
00:35:13,703 --> 00:35:15,331
No, don’t take it off.

601
00:35:15,331 --> 00:35:16,277
If you do, I’ll be mad at you.

602
00:35:18,663 --> 00:35:19,709
I’m going to buy some tissues.

603
00:35:20,024 --> 00:35:20,709
I have some.

604
00:35:23,153 --> 00:35:24,591
Then why did you act like
you were going to take your shirt off?

605
00:35:24,591 --> 00:35:25,211
Oh.

606
00:35:26,315 --> 00:35:29,692
Um, I thought that’d be cooler.

607
00:35:33,970 --> 00:35:35,135
Come with me.

608
00:35:35,529 --> 00:35:36,755
Come hang out at my house.

609
00:35:38,983 --> 00:35:39,729
Why should I go there?

610
00:35:45,079 --> 00:35:45,792
Well,

611
00:35:47,487 --> 00:35:51,308
I just want my house to be
a place where you can do anything.

612
00:35:52,491 --> 00:35:53,990
You can cry and be sad.

613
00:35:56,001 --> 00:35:57,483
There’s no one to be embarrassed around.

614
00:35:58,232 --> 00:35:59,820
I might be embarrassed around your brother.

615
00:36:01,022 --> 00:36:02,649
You can stay in my room.

616
00:36:05,152 --> 00:36:06,468
Fine. I’ll go.

617
00:36:11,153 --> 00:36:12,274
Where are my tissues?

618
00:36:13,417 --> 00:36:14,107
Oh.

619
00:36:16,670 --> 00:36:17,967
They’re with P’Cheewin.

620
00:36:20,924 --> 00:36:24,575
This is the first time Cheewa
has brought a friend home.

621
00:36:25,107 --> 00:36:26,361
It’s totally not normal.

622
00:36:27,071 --> 00:36:30,419
Even his best friend Jomyut
has never been there.

623
00:36:31,759 --> 00:36:35,408
But Jomyut and Newton
came to your birthday party.

624
00:36:36,374 --> 00:36:37,588
Cheewa!

625
00:36:37,805 --> 00:36:39,577
I was trying to set you up.

626
00:36:39,715 --> 00:36:41,362
Don’t sink the ship yet.

627
00:36:41,658 --> 00:36:42,515
What ship?

628
00:36:45,275 --> 00:36:46,377
A sailboat, I guess.

629
00:36:48,388 --> 00:36:50,693
I taught you how to flirt the other day.

630
00:36:50,988 --> 00:36:52,486
Haven’t you learned anything?

631
00:36:53,682 --> 00:36:54,474
P’Cheewin!

632
00:37:03,021 --> 00:37:04,660
Sorry. Slip of the tongue.

633
00:37:09,292 --> 00:37:12,393
Do you want me to keep my distance
so you brothers can talk freely?

634
00:37:13,773 --> 00:37:14,828
Just keep walking like this.

635
00:37:14,966 --> 00:37:15,647
It’s okay.

636
00:37:17,855 --> 00:37:19,806
Looks like it’s about to rain.

637
00:37:19,806 --> 00:37:20,969
Let’s hurry.

638
00:37:21,856 --> 00:37:23,019
Yeah, let’s go.

639
00:37:31,614 --> 00:37:33,984
Hey, make yourself at home, Niran.

640
00:37:34,313 --> 00:37:36,012
Okay. Thank you, P’Cheewin.

641
00:37:36,012 --> 00:37:36,721
Mm.

642
00:37:37,033 --> 00:37:38,398
Let’s go to my room.

643
00:37:40,113 --> 00:37:41,878
Here. Let me put your stuff away.

644
00:37:42,312 --> 00:37:43,203
Thank you.

645
00:37:47,993 --> 00:37:49,023
Can I use the bathroom first?

646
00:37:49,693 --> 00:37:50,439
Of course.

647
00:37:50,439 --> 00:37:51,141
Okay.

648
00:37:51,141 --> 00:37:51,831
That way.

649
00:38:04,832 --> 00:38:06,277
Please wait here.

650
00:38:30,376 --> 00:38:31,001
Wow.

651
00:38:35,200 --> 00:38:36,429
Do you want to play a game?

652
00:38:37,178 --> 00:38:38,127
There’s a game?

653
00:38:38,304 --> 00:38:39,053
Yes.

654
00:38:39,353 --> 00:38:40,339
Okay.

655
00:38:40,654 --> 00:38:41,893
But if you lose,

656
00:38:42,149 --> 00:38:44,061
you’d better not cry like a baby.

657
00:38:44,238 --> 00:38:46,971
You’re the only one crying.

658
00:38:49,179 --> 00:38:50,097
Watch it.

659
00:38:50,886 --> 00:38:52,834
But if I cry because I have a soft spot for you,

660
00:38:54,234 --> 00:38:56,163
please comfort me gently.

661
00:38:58,272 --> 00:39:00,430
What are you even saying?

662
00:39:01,081 --> 00:39:02,152
You little kid.

663
00:39:06,913 --> 00:39:07,995
Cheewa, step it up.

664
00:39:07,995 --> 00:39:08,753
I’m fighting.

665
00:39:08,753 --> 00:39:09,722
Do you even know how to play a game?

666
00:39:09,873 --> 00:39:11,110
Here.

667
00:39:11,110 --> 00:39:12,596
Here.

668
00:39:12,793 --> 00:39:13,348
Why are you smiling?

669
00:39:13,762 --> 00:39:14,842
Focus on the game.

670
00:39:14,842 --> 00:39:15,963
I am.

671
00:39:16,929 --> 00:39:18,659
I can’t with the way you said, “I am.”

672
00:39:18,659 --> 00:39:20,934
Hey, don’t pretend to lose!

673
00:39:22,018 --> 00:39:23,203
I’m not.

674
00:39:27,165 --> 00:39:28,432
I won't flick you anymore.

675
00:39:29,043 --> 00:39:30,291
Your nose is all red.

676
00:39:30,913 --> 00:39:32,043
Let me write on your face instead.

677
00:39:50,212 --> 00:39:52,355
Can you see when we’re this close?

678
00:39:55,312 --> 00:39:56,521
Not clearly.

679
00:39:59,419 --> 00:40:00,262
How about this close?

680
00:40:03,140 --> 00:40:04,125
It’s clear now.

681
00:40:05,307 --> 00:40:09,578
So you mean if we’re any farther apart,
you can’t see clearly anymore?

682
00:40:14,743 --> 00:40:18,647
Whether you can see clearly or not,
you’re getting your face painted.

683
00:40:23,871 --> 00:40:24,824
Aha.

684
00:40:30,039 --> 00:40:31,304
Let me ask you something.

685
00:40:31,462 --> 00:40:32,583
According to science,

686
00:40:33,569 --> 00:40:36,620
if I rub it a lot and the number shows up,
will I win the lottery if I buy that number?

687
00:40:38,098 --> 00:40:40,530
No, you won’t. That’s just superstition.

688
00:40:41,062 --> 00:40:41,763
Really?

689
00:40:44,227 --> 00:40:44,879
Mm.

690
00:40:46,614 --> 00:40:47,707
I think I’m enjoying this.

691
00:41:09,678 --> 00:41:11,036
I’m sorry.

692
00:41:12,357 --> 00:41:13,188
About what?

693
00:41:16,303 --> 00:41:18,463
I let you cry for so long.

694
00:41:19,311 --> 00:41:22,187
By the time I found you,
your eyes were all red.

695
00:41:27,352 --> 00:41:29,762
You were there all alone.

696
00:41:32,325 --> 00:41:35,685
I should’ve gone and sat next to you sooner.

697
00:41:44,226 --> 00:41:45,456
Why are you apologizing?

698
00:41:48,137 --> 00:41:49,650
It’s not your fault, Cheewa.

699
00:41:53,080 --> 00:41:55,449
I want to be by your side at a time like this.

700
00:41:57,617 --> 00:41:59,479
And I want you to know

701
00:42:00,011 --> 00:42:01,319
I’m here for you.

702
00:42:08,548 --> 00:42:10,490
Even though I’m not the hair on your head,

703
00:42:11,811 --> 00:42:13,575
I’m the one in your heart.

704
00:42:21,639 --> 00:42:22,334
Mm.

705
00:42:23,970 --> 00:42:24,851
Thanks.

706
00:42:31,474 --> 00:42:34,475
There’s a planet really far away from Earth.

707
00:42:36,328 --> 00:42:38,890
It’s farther away than you can imagine.

708
00:42:39,166 --> 00:42:41,125
It’s in a solid state.

709
00:42:44,003 --> 00:42:45,922
But what’s really special is

710
00:42:47,440 --> 00:42:51,995
it’s a solid that can absorb liquids really well.

711
00:42:53,927 --> 00:42:55,894
Today, I’m going to be that planet

712
00:42:56,820 --> 00:42:58,589
that helps absorb your tears.

713
00:43:00,442 --> 00:43:01,732
Will you let me?

714
00:43:02,047 --> 00:43:07,238
♪ Whenever you need me ♪

715
00:43:07,238 --> 00:43:11,289
♪ Just know I’m keeping you in my sight ♪

716
00:43:29,673 --> 00:43:31,256
The planet might be flooded, you know.

717
00:43:32,912 --> 00:43:35,063
Let this planet be flooded.

718
00:43:35,792 --> 00:43:37,175
We’ll float together.

719
00:43:41,003 --> 00:43:43,970
♪ And I’ll still be here ♪

720
00:43:43,970 --> 00:43:48,924
♪ Every turn, I’ll be near ♪

721
00:43:48,924 --> 00:43:53,221
♪ Even on starless nights ♪

722
00:43:53,359 --> 00:43:56,053
♪ I’ll be by your side ♪

723
00:43:56,053 --> 00:43:58,024
♪ Right here for life ♪

724
00:43:58,024 --> 00:44:03,119
♪ Just like you prayed to the stars ♪

725
00:44:03,119 --> 00:44:06,538
♪ I’ll be by your side ♪

726
00:44:41,313 --> 00:44:42,399
I’ll do it myself.

727
00:44:42,399 --> 00:44:44,247
I’ll find evidence to prove I’m not the bad guy.

728
00:44:44,247 --> 00:44:45,571
How will you proceed?

729
00:44:45,571 --> 00:44:47,652
Most of the time, Oy gets bullied when he passes the science building.

730
00:44:47,652 --> 00:44:49,122
So we have to lure them to the science building.

731
00:44:49,193 --> 00:44:50,994
But what if the real culprit is a ghost?

732
00:44:50,994 --> 00:44:52,662
We have to look for a ghost?

733
00:44:52,938 --> 00:44:54,251
P’Niran, are you okay?

734
00:44:54,251 --> 00:44:55,141
Are you worried about me?

735
00:44:55,141 --> 00:44:56,056
Did you know?

736
00:44:56,056 --> 00:44:59,987
If you keep beating around the bush,
you lose 20% of the time in your life.

737
00:44:59,987 --> 00:45:01,273
Hey, don’t get smart with me.
